PRODUCT FEATURES AND SPECIFICATIONS

Product:  Topaz for C, version 4.0
 
Manufacturer:  Software Science Inc.
               1818 Gilbreth Road, Suite 230,
               Burlingame, CA 94010-1213

Customer Service: (415) 697-0411,  Fax: (415) 697-1916,
Technical Support BBS (via modem): (415) 697-1624, or Voice: (510) 845-2110

Description:

TOPAZ is a C library of over 550 routines integrating a broad spectrum of
functions into a versatile programmer's tool-kit.  TOPAZ enables programmers
to write with "dBASE-like" syntax in C and use standard dBASE data files.
TOPAZ includes utilities, numerous programming examples and sample programs,
a dBASE-like report generator, and a template-based code generator.  TOPAZ
provides a powerful comprehensive platform from which you can quickly
develop applications of any type.  Both single-user and multi-user database
applications can be created.  In addition, the database engine portion of
the library can be used in Windows applications.

Features:

dBASE database file access with numerous high-level commands such as Use(),
Select(), Go(), GoTop(), GoBottom(), Skip(), Find(), Edit(), CopyTo(),
SayGet(), ReadGets(), SetFilterTo(),  SetRelationTo(), Browse(), EditMemo(),
ReportForm(), Append(), SetWhileTo(), AppendFrom(), Replace(),  etc.
Ascending, descending, and soundex indexes.  Fast full-database searches and
fast search and/or replace at the field level.  Database searches at a rate
of one million records per minute have been achieved. Relational database
systems may be created using any relational model. Multi-user support
includes record locking, file locking, append-only locking,  and programs
will operate with any MS-NET compatible network such as Novell NetWare,
3Com, Lantastic, Invisible Network, etc.  Unlike dBASE III+, Topaz
multi-user programs never prevent users from reading records or generating
reports even when other users have records or the file locked for update.
The Topaz exclusive ALock() function allows appending records to a file even
when other users have records locked for editing.

Sophisticated data entry routines provide easy multi-field editing with
unlimited data input validation at the individual field level.  Additional
input formatting with picture masks, range limits, color control and easy
field-by-field help specification is available.  Full featured text editor
functions are included for use with text files and memo fields.
Programmable access and manipulation of memo fields is also supported.

Numerous useful high-level routines are included for comprehensive date and
time math, print spooling, string manipulation, moving bar menus, dialog
boxes, pick and tag lists, progress bars, screen and window management,
pop-up calculator and calendar, screen savers, automatic and custom mouse
support, and much more. TOPAZ also includes support for screens produced
with the  Saywhat?! screen generator, also a product of Software Science
Inc.

Powerful utilities are provided including a template-based code generator, a
file definition/creation program, a report generator, a help system editor,
a dBASE file browser, end-user application color mapping utility, and a
database structure display utility.

Build complete context-sensitive help systems while you run your
application.  Even the end user can be allowed to create and/or edit the
help system.  Help screens may be moved around the screen at run-time so
that they don't obscure important information.

Topaz comes with over 800 pages of documentation including tutorial and
technical reference, dBASE to TOPAZ cross-reference, numerous code samples,
as well as sample programs and sample templates for the code generator.

